\ Exercises the well-known override marker under runtime-image AOT. The freshly-pushed marker must
\ compare equal to the one serialized onto the module word's definition: the image loader resolves
\ the serialized marker through lookupWellKnownMarker back to the static singleton, preserving
\ freeze->runtime pointer identity.
\
\ The marked word lives in a companion module because the image carries module words only; an
\ entry-file definition would not be serialized at all.

use "./support/override_marked.1z" ;

marked-word 42 = .
override override = .
"marked-word" word-markers [ override = ] #filter #count 0 > .
